### `<Plate>` prop API

```tsx
<Plate
  tone="dark"           // 'dark' | 'light' ΓÇö default 'dark'
  p="ms"                // prefix for gradient/pattern IDs within this plate
  title="Supplier catalogue ΓÇö raw to live"   // required
  sub="Hanicks ┬╖ one import pipeline"        // optional, default ''
  no="DO-ART-202"       // required ΓÇö refuses to render without it
  rev="01"              // optional, default '01'
  cls="DECODED OPS ┬╖ ISSUED"   // classification text, optional
>
  {/* children: page-specific inner SVG content (<g>, <path>, etc.) */}
</Plate>
```

### Token gaps resolved: **none needed**

`colors_and_type.css` (imported via `ds-marketing.css` ΓåÆ `ds-layer.css` ΓåÆ `layout.tsx`) already defines all tokens `ds-plates.css` references:
`--do-font-body`, `--do-font-heading`, `--do-font-mono`, `--do-space-*` (0ΓÇô32), `--do-text-xl`, `--do-tracking-wide`, `--do-weight-bold`, `--do-text-muted-on-dark`, `--do-text-secondary`, `--do-text-xs`, `--do-text-sm`, `--do-text-base`, `--do-leading-*`, `--do-radius-full`.

No changes to `globals.css` or any CSS file were needed.

### What changed vs the vanilla `ds-plates.js` approach

- **Before:** `DsPlatesLoader` dynamically imported `ds-plates.js`, which ran `document.querySelectorAll('svg.pl')` and injected frame HTML via `insertAdjacentHTML` ΓÇö a side-effect on React-managed DOM.
- **After:** `Plate.tsx` renders the frame declaratively in JSX with `useRef` + `useEffect` for IntersectionObserver. No DOM injection, no conflict with React's VDOM.
- The 3 homepage plates are all live `<Plate>` instances ΓÇö real, legitimate content on the homepage.

### Test plates left in place

